28:- `GET /` and `GET /app.js` serve the page (see Page).
29-- Any other path: 404 `not found`, whatever the method. This includes every path that starts with `/api/bookings/` and whose rest is empty or holds a `/`, such as `/api/bookings/` and `/api/bookings/1/`.
30-- A path above with a method not listed for it (HEAD and OPTIONS included): 405 `method not allowed`. For example `GET /api/bookings/abc` is 405. A 405 reply may or may not have an `Allow` header; it is not checked.
31-- Every reply with a body other than the page and the script has `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`. An error reply is `{"error": "<message>"}` with exactly that key, where `<message>` is the text given here.
32-
33-Booking rules (`POST /api/bookings`; the first rule that fails decides the reply)
34-1. The media type of the `Content-Type` header (the part before the first `;`, with spaces and tabs removed from both ends, letter case ignored) is not `application/json`, or the header is missing: 415 `content type must be application/json`.
35-2. The body is longer than 10000 bytes, counting the body bytes actually received: 413 `body too large`.
36-3. The body, decoded as `Buffer.prototype.toString('utf8')` does and then given to `JSON.parse`, is not a JSON object (it is empty, not valid JSON, `null`, an array, a string, a number or a boolean): 400 `body must be a JSON object`. Bytes that are not valid UTF-8 become U+FFFD and are not an error by themselves. A byte order mark at the very start is kept, so such a body is not valid JSON.
37-4. `room` is not a string equal to one of the room names (letter case matters): 400 `room must be one of Aurora, Borealis, Cosmos`.
38-5. `title` is not a string, or is shorter than 1 or longer than 80 UTF-16 code units after removing the whitespace at both ends (as `String.prototype.trim` does): 400 `title must be 1 to 80 characters`. The booking keeps the trimmed title.
39-6. `date` is not a string `YYYY-MM-DD` (4, 2 and 2 ASCII digits 0-9) naming a real day from 2000-01-01 to 2099-12-31, where February has 29 days in years divisible by 4: 400 `date must be a valid YYYY-MM-DD date`.
40-7. `start` is not a string `HH:MM` (2 and 2 ASCII digits 0-9) from `00:00` to `23:59`: 400 `start must be HH:MM`.
41-8. `end` is not such a string: 400 `end must be HH:MM`.
42-9. `end` is not later than `start`: 400 `end must be after start`.
43-10. The booking overlaps a booking of the same room on the same date, that is each of the two starts before the other ends (a booking may start exactly when another ends): 409 `room is already booked from <start> to <end>`, with the start and end of the overlapping booking that starts earliest.
44-- No field except `title` is trimmed or changed: ` 2026-11-03`, `2026-11-3` and `9:00` are invalid.
45-
46:Page
47-- `GET /` answers 200 with `Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8` and the page. `GET /app.js` answers 200 with `Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8` and the page's script.
48-- The page loads the script with a `<script>` element whose `src` is exactly `/app.js`, with no `type`, `defer` or `async` attribute, placed as the last element in `<body>`. The script is a classic script (no `import` or `export`) and does its setup at once, without waiting for any load event.
49-- All of the page's code is in `/app.js`: the page has no inline script and no `on...` event attributes. Neither the page nor the script contains `http://` or `https://`.
50-- Of the browser's APIs, the script uses only `fetch` (with the `method`, `headers` and `body` options, and the reply's `status` and `json()`), `document.getElementById`, `document.createElement`, the `textContent`, `value`, `type`, `disabled`, `append`, `replaceChildren` and `addEventListener` members of elements, and `preventDefault` of events.
51-- The HTML elements named below are checked by their tag, attributes and text, not by exact markup: attribute order, quoting and extra attributes are free.
52-- The page's `<title>` and its only `<h1>` both have the text `Room bookings`.
53-- The page holds a `<form id="booking-form">` with the `novalidate` attribute. Inside it are `<select id="room" name="room">`, `<input type="text" id="title" name="title">`, `<input type="date" id="date" name="date">`, `<input type="time" id="start" name="start">`, `<input type="time" id="end" name="end">`, and `<button type="submit" id="book">` with the text `Book`. Each of the five fields has its own `<label for="<id>">`, which does not contain the field, with exactly this text: `Room` for `#room`, `Title` for `#title`, `Date` for `#date`, `Start` for `#start`, `End` for `#end`.
54-- Outside the form, the page holds `<input type="date" id="filter-date">` with its own `<label for="filter-date">`, which does not contain it, with exactly the text `Show date`; `<button type="button" id="show-all">` with the text `Show all`; `<ul id="booking-list">`; and `<p id="error" role="alert">`, which is empty.
55-- Every value is shown as plain text, never as HTML: a title `<b>x</b>` shows those 8 characters.
56-- Requests use path-only URLs exactly as written here: `/api/rooms`, `/api/bookings`, `/api/bookings?date=<value>` and `/api/bookings/<id>`.
57-- A reply has an error status when its status is not the success status of its request: 200 for `GET`, 201 for `POST` and 204 for `DELETE`. The reply's error message is the body's `error` value when the body is a JSON object whose `error` is a string, and `Request failed.` otherwise. A reply other than a 204 whose body cannot be read or parsed as JSON counts as no reply. A request that gets no reply at all (for example because the server is down) shows `Could not reach the server.` in `#error`, except for an earlier list fetch, as said below.
58-- Rooms: the HTML holds no `<option>` element and none of the room names. When the page loads, the script requests `GET /api/rooms` and fills `#room` with one `<option>` per room, in that order, whose value and text are the room name. If that request gets an error status, `#error` shows the reply's error message and `#room` stays empty; with no reply, `#error` shows `Could not reach the server.` and `#room` stays empty. The first list fetch starts at page load too, without waiting for the rooms reply.
59:- The list: when the page loads, and each time the Page rules say the list is fetched again, the script requests `GET /api/bookings`, adding `?date=<value>` (the value unchanged) while the value of `#filter-date` is not empty, and replaces the content of `#booking-list` with one `<li>` per booking in the reply's order. Each `<li>` has exactly two child nodes: a text node with exactly the text `<date> <start>-<end> <room>: <title>` and no trailing space (for example `2026-11-03 09:00-10:00 Aurora: Standup`), then a `<button type="button">` with the text `Cancel`. With no bookings, the list holds a single `<li>` whose only child is a text node `No bookings.`.
60-- A list fetch that gets an error status shows the reply's error message in `#error` and leaves the list as it was; one that gets no reply shows `Could not reach the server.` and leaves the list as it was; one that succeeds leaves `#error` alone. When list fetches overlap, only the outcome of the last one started is used: the outcome of every earlier one, an error status or no reply included, changes neither the list nor `#error`.
61-- Booking: a submit event on the form never reloads the page (the script calls `preventDefault`). A submit while `Book` is disabled sends nothing. Otherwise the script disables `Book`, then sends `POST /api/bookings` with exactly the header `Content-Type: application/json` and a JSON body whose keys `room`, `title`, `date`, `start` and `end` hold the five controls' current values unchanged (the title is not trimmed). The script never checks the fields itself. `Book` is enabled again as soon as the request settles (the reply and its body have arrived, or the request failed), before anything else happens. On 201 the `title` control is emptied (the others keep their values), `#error` is emptied and the list is fetched again. On any other status `#error` shows the reply's error message exactly (for example `room is already booked from 09:00 to 10:00`). With no reply `#error` shows `Could not reach the server.`. In both of these cases the form and the list stay as they were.
62-- Cancel: clicking a `Cancel` button disables it and sends `DELETE /api/bookings/<id>` for its booking; the button is enabled again when the request settles. On 204 `#error` is emptied; on any other status `#error` shows the reply's error message (for example `booking not found` when the booking was already gone). After either of these, the list is fetched again. With no reply, `#error` shows `Could not reach the server.` and the list is not fetched again.
63-- Filter: a `change` event on `#filter-date` fetches the list again at once; the `input` event does nothing. `Show all` sets the value of `#filter-date` to the empty string and fetches the list again once, without dispatching any event.
